<h2 class="wp-block-heading block-personal-note__title" id="h-a-taste-of-mediterranean-beyond-the-classic-chicken-salad">A Taste of Mediterranean &ndash; Beyond the Classic Chicken Salad</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image alignright is-resized is-style-rounded"><img decoding="async" width="600" height="600" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul.jpg" alt="Aysegul Sanford from the front view." class="wp-image-84391" style="width:200px;height:200px" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul.jpg 600w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul-400x400.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul-150x150.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul-500x500.jpg 500w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul-300x300.jpg 300w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul-96x96.jpg 96w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul-378x378.jpg 378w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul-276x276.jpg 276w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/aysegul.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In Turkiye, savory yogurt is not just a side dish; it is a staple served with nearly every meal. Growing up, <strong>Tzatziki</strong> (or <strong><em>Cac&#305;k</em></strong>, as we call it) was a constant on our table, especially as a cooling balance to spicy charred kebab dishes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I developed this recipe to provide a high-protein meal that is quick to assemble, built on the same foundation as my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/easy-to-make-tzatziki-sauce-recipe/">Homemade Tzatziki Sauce</a>. It stores beautifully and can even be made a day in advance, making it the perfect solution for busy weekdays.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Why This Authentic Version Works:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>The Crunch &amp; Aromatics:</strong> While the Tzatziki base is creamy and flavorful, I knew that simply mixing it with chicken wouldn&rsquo;t be enough. To give it a proper &ldquo;salad&rdquo; texture, I added thinly sliced radishes, crispy cucumbers, chopped scallions, and fresh herbs. I also sprinkled it with a pinch of sumac (optional) for a unique, tart finish.</li>



<li><strong>The No-Mayo Solution:</strong> Unlike most American chicken salads, this recipe uses zero mayonnaise. It might come as a surprise, but the combination of garlic, lemon, and Greek yogurt creates a punchy, satisfying texture that rivals any traditional dressing.</li>
</ul>

</div>

